{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Finding (audit of epic 3405-c0b7)\n**Site:** the gate degrade producers in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` — `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (via the `except (LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` arm at line 203), `_degraded_code_review_verdict` (line ~336 sets `\"llm_unavailable\": True`), and the completion-verdict degrade. They emit `coverage.llm_unavailable = True`.\n\n**Problem:** the arm catches `(LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` together (comment at line 203 folds `LLMInputRejectedError`, bug 43d4, into \"the mid-run infra outage\" arm). So when the cause is an INPUT REJECTION (oversized/malformed prompt, content-policy refusal), the verdict still carries `coverage.llm_unavailable=True`. The field's docstring admits the name is overloaded to mean \"no provider record accompanies this verdict\" (degraded), NOT literally \"the provider is down\".\n\n**Wrong signal:** `coverage.llm_unavailable=True` for a non-availability fault. `resolution_fields(outcome)` DOES ride the truthful `resolution_class` (CHANGE_INPUT) alongside, so the disposition is recoverable — but the boolean's NAME misreports the cause.\n\n**Consumers that branch on the boolean:** `plan_review/drift_floor.py:202`, `plan_review/orchestrator.py:468`, `review_bot/adapter.py:114`.\n\n**Observable vs latent:** OBSERVABLE — on every degraded gate verdict JSON and to the three consumers above.\n\n**Proposed fix (needs decision):** behavior-change / rename — either split the flag (a neutral `degraded` / `no_provider_record` boolean vs a strict `llm_unavailable` reserved for real outages) or have consumers/readers key off `resolution_class` instead of the overloaded boolean. Affects the verdict contract and three consumers → **escalate**.\n\n**caused_by / class:** the same \"input-rejection framed as provider outage\" pattern; origin 8a31 / bug 43d4.\n\n## Operator decision (approved: Option B)\nSplit the overloaded `coverage.llm_unavailable` boolean: keep it True ONLY for genuine availability outages; add a distinct `input_rejected` signal for `LLMInputRejectedError`. Do NOT introduce a broad `degraded`/`no_provider_record` category (operator explicitly rejected it).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A single source-of-truth helper `degrade_cause_flags(error)` in `src/rebar/llm/failure.py` returns mutually-exclusive coverage flags — `input_rejected=True` for `LLMInputRejectedError`, else `llm_unavailable=True` (real outages and the string-error degrade tail).\n- [x] Both degrade builders emit the split signal through that helper: `_degraded_code_review_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`) and `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py`).\n- [x] The three readers honor the split: `plan_review/drift_floor.py` (veto branch), `plan_review/orchestrator.py` (maps `input_rejected` to INDETERMINATE), and `review_bot/adapter.py` (non-retryable `input-rejected` coverage-gap reason, deliberately NOT in `RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS` — a deterministic input rejection is an honest fail-closed veto, not a deferred retry).\n- [x] `coverage.llm_unavailable` is no longer True for an input-rejection fault; the new `input_rejected` flag carries it instead, preserving real-outage behavior unchanged.\n- [x] A held-out oracle proves the split through the real surfaces (helper contract, string-error edge, plan-review E2E, all three readers); checked: `python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96.py tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96_heldout.py -q` passes.\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96.py tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96_heldout.py -q`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788077321698692001,"uuid":"ba00b742-f817-4a07-b37a-f65ffc8b91fb"}